      {
        "review_id": 685440523,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r685440523-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Hindu Temple,Some never Leave",
        "text": "Pashupatinath Hindu temple not far from the airport which is hidden thankfully by a forrest, one of Hindu's most holy sites.Built over a large temple complex which some you can enter and some area's are for Hindu's only.There are a couple of walkways to the entrance the main having a long avenue of food and souvenir shops to by pass,its 1000 rup to enter the temple grounds but like i said you cant go everywhere,but what you can see is quite historic/cultural/and slightly horrific to some.There is two sides to the temple grounds ,each side of the river of souls/Bagmati river,Which you can cross via the bridge.There are Hindu temples and a mother Theresa sanctuary,very close to the ceramonial burning platforms on the rivers edge,yes !!, Hindu people use this as there final place before ritual burnings that are done in full view of anybody that is there ,usually its family members and they must stay untill the body is fully consumed and emptied into the river.To some it can be a horrific sight but its done everyday and night ,and on the opposite side of the bridge ( Same side )is where the well off/Politicians and royalty are burned/consumed they cannot mix with ordinary folk. you may see the coffins been washed in the river to reuse,and people looking through the ashes that are emptied into the river for any gold that was in the bodies.Across the river you get the better sights of the temple area as its built higher and gives some scenic views,you will come across lots of smaller temples,and Sadhus holy men who follow Shiva,there is a really good avenue/optical illusion of Lingas and Yoni's which seem to go on for ever , very cleverly built.On some of the temple walls there is a lot of sexual carvings of men/women which you find in many Hindu temples.Also Some nice wall murals/paintings and lots of monkeys looking for food from tourists.This Temple complex will open your eyes up one way or another,there is a lot of cuture/history and tradition here , well worth a visit ,but not for everybody, oh and watch out for the bulls, they are quite large here.",
