        "title": "An interesting cultural Hindu Temple to visit in Kathmandu",
        "text": "The Pashupatinath is an Hindu temple located in Kathmandu, that has a very large in area which you can access most of the area (there is an area with access restricted only to religious that tourists do not access), among traditional religious constructions of different sizes among trees and dozens of monkeys circulating around (be aware not to have food in your hands because monkeys The monkeys will want to take it out of your hands anyway and with this they may inadvertently hurt you. There in Pashupatinathyou will find a good and interesting experience of Hindu tradition and culture. On june 2019 I paid 1000,00 nepalese rupies for the entrance (about  nine US dollars). I thought the place in general, especially as it is an important Hindu temple, should be more careful in terms of cleanliness. There were a lot of garbage and neglected parts of the structure in general that should be better taken care of because of their historical, cultural and religious value.",
